// Senodonnos, a magistrate of Avaricum. One of those who knelt to the council
// to spare the city when the rest were burned (Caesar BG VII.15).
=== start
[flag senod_met] -> again
~ set senod_met
[!flag scorched_earth] A big man in a blue cloak, at a table covered in tally sticks, under a roof painted red and gold. "Senodonnos. I sit on the council, for my sins." He waves at a stool. "Welcome to Avaricum. Have you seen the wall? Everyone should see the wall."
[flag scorched_earth, !flag avaricum_siege] A big man in a blue cloak, with ash on it. He's been out to the burned towns. "Senodonnos, of the council. Twenty towns in a day, my own farms among them. And this one spared, because I knelt in the mud in front of the whole council and begged." He touches his gold torque. "I'd do it again. I think I'd do it again."
[flag avaricum_siege] A big man in a blue cloak gone grey with mud. He looks as if he hasn't slept. "You came in through the marsh? Then you're very brave or very stupid, and either way we need you. Senodonnos, of the council. What's left of it."
-> hub

=== again
[flag avaricum_siege] "Still here. Good. So is the wall."
[!flag avaricum_siege] "Back again. What can the council do for you?"
-> hub

=== hub
* [quest factor=found, !flag avaricum_siege, item factor_list] Show him the Aeduan's tablet of names. -> expose
* [quest factor=found, !flag avaricum_siege, speech 50] "Your Aeduan grain buyer is pricing your households for the slave market. Search his lodging." -> expose
* [quest factor active, flag avaricum_siege] "The Aeduan grain buyer, Epomeduos." -> factor_left
* [item aeduan_letter, !flag letter_read] "Can you read this?" -> letter
* "Tell me about the city." -> city
* [flag scorched_earth] "Why spare Avaricum and burn the rest?" -> spared
* [flag avaricum_siege] "How long can the city hold?" -> hold
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== expose
~ set factor_gone; quest factor done_exposed done; give aeduan_letter; silver 50; standing bituriges 15; renown 2
[item factor_list] He reads the tablet twice. The second time he finds his own house on it, near the top, and the price beside it. He doesn't say anything for a while. Then he calls for his men.
[!item factor_list] He hears you out without a word, then sends four men to the lodging behind the forum. They come back with the Aeduan and his strongbox, and in the strongbox is a tablet of names. Senodonnos finds his own house on it, near the top.
[item factor_list] ~ take factor_list

By evening Epomeduos has been taken to the wall, and there is one less stranger in Avaricum. Senodonnos sends you what was found on him: a little silver, and a sealed tablet. "It's addressed to Noviodunum," he says. "I don't want it in my house. I think you want it in yours."
-> hub

=== factor_left
"Epomeduos? He went out of the south gate the day before the Romans came, with his mule and his tablets." Senodonnos laughs without much in it. "Somebody always knows before the rest of us. It's usually somebody with a tablet."
-> hub

=== letter
~ set letter_read; known noviodunum; xp 50
[quest factor active, flag factor_gone] ~ quest factor done_killed done
[quest factor active] ~ quest factor done_stolen done
[quest hostages=find_tally] ~ quest hostages north
[quest hostages=read_tally] ~ quest hostages north
[quest hostages=ask_riders] ~ quest hostages north
He breaks the seal, reads, and reads it to you, frowning. "Dannotalos of the Aedui, to the keeper of the gate at Noviodunum: the bearer is his. Let him in and out, show him the pens and whatever is in them on Dannotalos's account, and don't trouble the Roman quartermaster about it."
[flag factor_turned] "And something at the bottom in another hand. The bearer's partner, likewise." He looks up at you. "Partner."
He hands it back as if it were dirty. "The Aedui are Rome's brothers, they say. They sell their brothers too, I suppose."
-> hub

=== city
"The richest city in Gaul, and the best defended." He says it the way other men say their own names. "River on the north, marsh round the rest, and one narrow road in from the south, with a wall across it that no ram has ever broken. Iron from our own pits, furnaces day and night. Wine from the Greeks, salt from the sea, and everybody passing through pays toll." He spreads his hands. "We're very rich. It hasn't made us very wise, but it's made us very rich."
-> hub

=== spared
He looks at the tally sticks for a long time.

"The king wanted it burned with the rest. Leave Caesar nothing, he said. Not a loaf. He was right, and I knew he was right, and I knelt in front of every chief in the council and begged them not to make us burn the most beautiful city in Gaul with our own hands. It can hold, I said. River and marsh, one road in. Easy to defend." He touches the torque. "The king said no, and then he looked at us all on our knees, and he said yes. Out of pity, I think. He's young."

"If it holds, I'll have been right. Every morning I go up on the wall to find out."
-> hub

=== hold
"We have food for a while. The Romans don't. Their grain comes up from the Aedui and the Boii, and the Aedui are slow and the Boii are poor, and the king burns everything for twenty miles around them. They're eating their cattle." He rubs his eyes. "They should have given up by now. Every morning I go up on the wall to see if they've gone."
[flag terrace_fire] "The terrace is nearly at the wall. The miners set it on fire last night, and the Romans put it out. They always put it out."
-> hub
